      Both: Pranksters.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 9 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 9.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240917210430-03'00')/NM(bb138ce29a0f43518600d4a0c15c9228)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">         Director: Stoic, but Innocent.&#13;         Janitor: Energic and Carefree&#13;         Both: Pranksters.</span></p></body>)/Rect[210.765 259.263 397.965 290.885]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj48 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(This entity consists of a rotating chalkboard, with a front and a back face, total height of 5ê9êê, and total length of 5ê2êê, considering its frame support, dated approximately from 1925 and donated by the CUC to help the çExponential Knowledgeé middle a\nd high school. After incidents where Morse Code messages were found written on the object, always leading to some kind of prank or some dead end, the college docents started looking for an author, to no avail and ultimately decided to install cameras in \and around the institution. To this day, no other messages were discovered. The truth: The board has two consciences, one for each face, who act together. Their origins, composition and motivations are completely unknown, and for some reason, they call th\emselves the çDirectoré and the çJanitoré, although not having any links to the real director or janitor of the high school.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Arial 10 Tf)/DS(font: Arial,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240917210656-03'00')/NM(d7acb930cdb148c288da8a71ac95f1c3)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">This entity consists of a rotating chalkboard, with a front and a back face, total height of 5&#8217;9&#8217;&#8217;, and total length of 5&#8217;2&#8217;&#8217;, consi\dering its frame support, dated approximately from 1925 and donated by the CUC to help the &#8220;Exponential Knowledge&#8221; middle and high school. After incidents where Morse Code messages were found written on the object, always leading to some kind \of prank or some dead end, the college docents started looking for an author, to no avail and ultimately decided to install cameras in and around the institution. To this day, no other messages were discovered. The truth: The board has two consciences, on\e for each face, who act together. Their origins, composition and motivations are completely unknown, and for some reason, they call themselves the &#8220;Director&#8221; and the &#8220;Janitor&#8221;, although not having any links to the real director or\ janitor of the high school.</span></p></body>)/Rect[45.3301 100.864 571.302 206.874]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj49 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(    6)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240909154137-03'00')/NM(1136aaeffc294a48afa27816b1ee9af3)/Page 2/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:21.8pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">    6</span></p></body>)/Rect[17.301 674